WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.980
A woman's uterus grows to over 500 times

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.050
its normal size during pregnancy.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.780
But not all changes are visible.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:13.543
In fact, some of the biggest
changes happen in her brain.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.480
When a mother sees her
newborn for the first time,

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.300
it's love at first sight, literally.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.680
That's because once she gives birth,

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.720
core regions of her brain's
reward network kick in.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.370
They signal the release
of feel-good hormones

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.440
like dopamine and oxytocin into her blood,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.530
which immediately triggers
a strong connection

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:45.310
of love and devotion to her newborn.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.710
In fact, studies show that recent mothers

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:51.040
have similar levels of
oxytocin as romantic couples

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:52.223
who are newly in love.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.490
And human moms aren't alone here.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.600
Scientists discovered that rodents

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.830
got a bigger kick of dopamine
from feeding their pups

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.240
than from receiving injections of cocaine.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.960
What's more, brain scans
reveal that a human mom

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.190
has a similar experience when
she sees her infant smiling.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:14.880
But it's a different story
when her baby is crying.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.040
Those cries activate a
network in the mom's brain

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.890
known as the emotion regulation network.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:24.400
It includes the prefrontal
and cingulate control systems,

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.740
which help control her emotions.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.480
And that's important since
it can be easy to lose

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.200
your temper when you're
running on very little sleep

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.430
and are distressed by the baby's cries.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.080
And while motherhood can be exhausting,

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.480
new moms are actually
more alert than normal

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:44.630
thanks to their brain's salience network.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:48.450
Scientists think giving birth
activates this network to help

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:52.530
a mother detect threats and
protect her infant from harm,

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.210
especially in dangerous situations

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:58.800
when that network can
help ramp up adrenaline.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.520
But on a daily basis,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.720
Mom needs to understand
her newborn's needs.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.660
To accomplish that, she uses empathy,

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.750
which comes from her
brain's social network.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:13.060
It involves the insular and amygdala,

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.560
which researchers found became more active

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.630
when moms looked at photos of their babies

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:20.960
in distress compared to neutral photos.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:24.060
But it's not just the
mom's brain that changes.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.220
Research shows that a dad's
brain releases oxytocin

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:30.950
when he interacts with his baby too.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.890
This is often accompanied by a surge

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.800
of another hormone: prolactin.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.540
It's often called the milk
hormone because it triggers

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.840
the production of breast milk,

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.440
but men can produce it too,

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.330
and researchers have found that dads

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.470
who frequently played with their babies

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:50.160
had higher prolactin levels in their blood

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.120
than fathers who didn't.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.133
They were also more responsive
to their baby's cries.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:03:00.240
So in the end, having a
child is a big change.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.603
Not just for your lifestyle,
for your brain too.

